    "rich_text_p7D8ce": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "spacer_L8mYri": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        },
        "heading_MrGjAB": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "FAQ",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "heading_font_class": "fs-heading-3-base"
          }
        },
        "border_JMAjFR": {
          "type": "border",
          "settings": {}
        },
        "subheading_jRWLhL": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What is the difference between the 6\" x 6\" and 6\" x 8\" multi-wick pillar candles?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_cVFhCr": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The 6\" x 6\" size works better when you want a large focal candle without adding too much height. The 6\" x 8\" version gives you a taller, fuller statement and makes more sense on larger consoles, entry tables, mantels, and other surfaces that need more candle presence.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_ykeVbb": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_fVaWkq": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "When should I choose a multi-wick pillar instead of a standard pillar candle?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_xVMDY7": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose a multi-wick pillar when one candle needs to carry the arrangement on its own. Our Bolsius 3-wick pillars are a better fit for larger focal areas than smaller single-wick pillars because they bring more scale and a stronger visual anchor right away.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_68L9WH": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_63Jihh": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Are these multi-wick pillars meant for everyday décor or larger statement areas?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_dttHE3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>They make the most sense in larger statement areas. With only 6\" x 6\" and 6\" x 8\" 3-wick formats in this range, these are stronger choices for mantels, entry tables, event displays, and fuller centerpiece work than for small casual tables.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_7QXgMW": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_TCpCmP": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Do your multi-wick pillar candles come in more than one color?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_zpDMyy": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Right now, this assortment is focused on ivory. That makes it easier to build a warm, consistent look when you want a large focal candle and do not want to sort through several color variations.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_T6Cpcf": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_C6d8PF": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Can I pair both multi-wick sizes in one arrangement?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_Nq7qRa": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes, the two sizes work well together when you want one arrangement with more height and depth. A 6\" x 8\" pillar can take the lead while the 6\" x 6\" version supports it without breaking the ivory color match.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_dTL4pf": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_8nYt8z": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "How should I style a multi-wick pillar so it feels finished?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_VH7yLh": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Use it where there is room around it, and give it a sturdy base, such as a tray, pedestal, or wider holder. These larger 3-wick pillars look best when the surface does not feel crowded, and the candle has enough space to read as the main decorative element.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_dpe9RU": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_MehrQH": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Are these a good fit for warm-toned interiors and event décor?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_zhjM6a": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes, they are a strong fit for warm-toned interiors because this range is entirely ivory. That softer tone works naturally with cream textiles, wood surfaces, brass accents, and event palettes that feel richer or warmer than crisp white. </p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_fmx8zR": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_zG33aG": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What is the best use for a multi-wick pillar candle?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_wGfWWF": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A multi-wick pillar candle from Kisco Candles works best as a focal piece on a mantel, console, entry table, or larger centerpiece. The wider format and three-wick design give it more presence than a standard pillar, so it does not need much around it to feel substantial.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        }
      },
